NPL-it is a field of artificial intelligence and computer science that focuses on enabling computers to understand, interpret ,\
generate and interact with human language

How NPL works
1. Text preprocessing- It includes cleaning a preparing text by removing punctuations and tokenizing it 
2. Language understanding- Analyzing grammer and understand the meaning and context
3. ML or DL ( Model training)- Training models on large amount of text to recognize patterns
4. Generating text- Producing reports and predictions 

some common NLP applications include
1. Machine translation- Translating English to japanese
2. chatbots and virtual assistants- eg. chatgpt , siri etc
3. Sentiment analysis - determining whether the review is positive or not
4. Text summarization- generate a summary from a text document
5. spam detection- filtering unwanted emails
6. speech recognition- converting spoken words into text
7. Information retrievel- search engines
8. Conversational agents- eg swiggy's helpline and query agents
9. Knowledge graphs and QA systems- big database- connect entities to make a large knowledge graph- transtale into questions and answers
10. Topic Modelling- automatically finding hidden topics in a collection of text documents
11. Text Generation- finding the next word based on your previous typing behaviour
12. Text Parsing- gramatically brekdown the sentence to understand the meaning

Approaches to NLP
1. Heuristic approach- It is a mental shortcut that people sue to solve problems and make judgements quickly and efficiently but 
that is not always optimal and perfect. Instead of learning from data like machine learning technique , heuristic approaches rely 
on human defined rules

Common heuristic techniques
1. spell checking
2. keyword checking
3. pattern checking
4. chatbots
5. grammer checking
6. Dictionary lookup

Advantage-
1. Easy to understand and implement
2. Fast execution
3. No training data required

Disadvantage-
1. Rules are written manually
2. difficult to maintain as the numbe of rules grow
3. doesn't adapt to new data
4. poor at handling context

Three important NLP concets that heuristic technique uses
1. Regular expresions- It is a pattern used to match, search,extract, replace the text, and often used for text preprocessing and
Information extraction.
2. WordNet- it is a laxcal database of english developed at princeton university that represent the relationship between words such 
as synonyms, antonyms, hypernyms, hyponyms
2 Open minded commen sense- It is a project that collected everyday commen sense knowledge from humans and make it available for 
computers

